WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.500
If you want to see some evidence for the possibility
of a Stephen King cinematic universe, stick

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.680
around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:14.969
This shot was in teasers but I actually noticed
something new, you can see the crew and production

00:00:14.969 --> 00:00:16.620
truck in the reflection here.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.520
And speaking of reflections, remember how
I pointed out that there were no eyes in Pennywise's

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.110
reflection in the water, and said it may have
just been an unfinished visual effect that

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.470
would be added before the movie was released?

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.570
Well it looks like they have gone and added
that into this trailer.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.320
Because as you can see, eyes should reflect
on water.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.340
Here we see the lucky 7 all together in what
is presumably the barrens the place where

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.060
they hang out and build a fort to hide out
from Henry Bower's gang of bullies.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:43.410
This has got to be the scene where they can
make the Promise.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.270
If you're not familiar with the story, the
book begins with Mike Hanlon as an adult,

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:50.670
calling all the childhood friends to remind
them of the promise they made: that they would

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.840
return to Derry if IT were to ever come back.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.160
Mike is holding his wrist in an awkward way.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.790
It might be nothing, but I feel like it could
be that how wrist got hurt during the rock

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.750
fight with Henry Bowers gang.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:02.930
This is a nice touch.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:06.829
Before we saw a missing poster for Patrick
Hockstetter, but we weren't sure if that was

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:10.570
just an easter egg from the book, or if Patrick
was going to be an actual character.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:14.200
Looks like he's going to be a part of it,
as the face is seen here along with what I

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.220
assume is Belch Huggins, Henry Bowers, which
is kind of confirmed because Henry has a knife

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.159
just like this in the book, and possibly Victor
Chris.

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:25.520
Even before this trailer dropped I had begun
to suspect that Patrick's story would be documented

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.520
in this new movie when I saw an article talking
about how IT would be taking advantage of

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.930
it's R-rating in ways that the mini series
just wasn't able to as a TV program.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.910
I think if you're going to remake, reboot
or readapt something, you should have a good

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:42.420
reason for it, other than just money and making
a darker IT movie in order to to do justice

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.990
to the disturbing nature of the source material
is a green light in my book.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.600
I'm not saying it's my book.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.659
It's Stephen King's book.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:52.049
I don't want to start that whole thing again.

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:56.070
Belch is wearing an Anthrax shirt, which is
interesting, because in the book, which is

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:59.740
set in the 50s rather than the 80s, one of
the few things that all of the kids seem to

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:04.939
agree on, Lucky 7 and Bowers Gang alike, is
their love for rock and roll; a love that

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:08.680
is not shared with seemingly any of the adults
in Derry.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.840
That becomes kind of a motif, a symbolic representation,
of Pennywise's reign of terror in Derry.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.349
Adults are in denial and kind of turn a blind
eye to the reality of the situation because

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:22.599
they are afraid of change, whether it be the
rise of rock &amp; roll in the 50's, or the rise

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.319
of an evil being in their town.

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:28.310
So now with this being set in the 80s, maybe
metal serves that purpose now.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.799
I certainly wouldn't mind seeing Richie jamming
out to Madhouse.

00:02:31.799 --> 00:02:36.860
This Derry Newspaper is from 1908, one of
my personal favorite years in history, and

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.650
there is an article about the Iron Works Explosion.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.840
So it would seem that despite moving up the
timeline involving our main characters, Derry's

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.389
past history has only shifted two years (it's
1906 in the book).

00:02:47.389 --> 00:02:48.389
It's also a publication from July 4th, and
in this shot in the trailer, there seems to

00:02:48.389 --> 00:02:49.389
be some kind of Independence Day Festival
going on in the background.

00:02:49.389 --> 00:02:52.249
This is just speculation, but I'm thinking
something bad happens on the anniversary of

00:02:52.249 --> 00:02:53.749
the Iron Works disaster.

00:02:53.749 --> 00:02:56.659
The book Ben is reading is called A History
of Derry.

00:02:56.659 --> 00:02:57.939
He also has a cassette player.

00:02:57.939 --> 00:03:00.590
Look at the wallpaper behind Bill.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:01.939
Circus animals.

00:03:01.939 --> 00:03:05.739
Pennywise actually does have ancient ties
to a circus in the story, which is where he

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:07.950
got his name, Pennywise the Dancing Clown.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:12.469
This whole basement scene is a pretty dark
in this shot, so let's turn up the lights.

00:03:12.469 --> 00:03:15.930
In the corner there are some oars, and there's
also a life vest on the wall.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:19.780
I wonder if these choices have anything to
do with the fact that Georgie dies while playing

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.040
with a paper boat, because he does appear
in this scene as an apparition.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.319
Here's another dark scene.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:26.590
Lumos Maxima!

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.420
Ok, this is creepy.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:31.010
First thing I noticed is Pennywise sinking
into the well.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.120
If Ringu didn't make wells creepy enough for
you it looks like the clown's got you covered.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.510
There is also a hand on the side here, maybe
one of the kids pushing open a door.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.950
Scattered on the floor are children's clothes
and toys.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.629
This looks like an elephant, another circus
animal.

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:49.610
I know I said this adaptation would be darker,
but children's clothing?

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.129
This could be a lot more messed up than I
thought.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:55.170
It's also shown in this other shot right here.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.359
And there's also a nuise hanging from the
rafter.

00:03:57.359 --> 00:04:00.819
This room full of various clowns has a few
things that I loved.

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:03.180
I'll turn up the lights again for you to make
it easier to see.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.560
This little guy right here is a nice throwback
to the Tim Curry Pennywise design from the

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.579
1990 TV miniseries.

00:04:08.579 --> 00:04:13.580
At first, I didn't notice this clown's head
turning to follow Eddie as he walks.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.699
It's good to see something subtle like that
and know it's not just all jumpscares.

00:04:17.699 --> 00:04:19.670
Bill wears a Tracker Bros t-shirt in this
shot.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:23.540
It's a nice little easter egg referencing
the Tracker Bros shipping company, a family

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:25.940
owned trucking service in Derry from the book.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.780
I'm really impressed by the level of detail
in this film.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:33.030
Like the inclusion of Mr Keene, the pharmacist
who supplies Eddie with his inhalers.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:35.460
Or the Glowing Yellow Eyes of the clown.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:39.590
Some people theorized in my comment section
on the previous videos that this IT movie

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:44.190
could be tied in with The Dark Tower movie
that is coming out this year and also based

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.680
off of a Stephen King novel.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.560
The movies aren't being made by the same studio
and I wasn't really a believer that there

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:54.170
could be a Stephen King cinematic universe
for that reason, as cool as it might sound,

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.360
but since then I have noticed some possible
clues pointing to one.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.230
I definitely wouldn't say anything is confirmed,
and some of these are a little bit of a reach,

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.530
but I'm going to show you what I noticed,
and you can put your own findings in the comments.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.860
Smith Coronna is a typewriter company.

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:10.550
The typewriter is a very important prop in
The Shining.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.290
I already mentioned the Christine shirt in
my other video.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:18.010
Then there's this newspaper headline that
says "No indictment yet in the Gillespie..."

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.160
and I wasn't able to read anything past that.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.720
Gillespie is a character in Salem's Lot.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.110
In fact, he's a cop.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:28.950
By the way, did this shot kind of remind anyone
of Salem's Lot?

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:33.060
But the biggest thing for me is this Dark
Tower trailer that came out YESTERDAY.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.320
In the title of the video are the words "connected
KINGdom".

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:40.370
It starts with an animation taking us through
the Overlook Hotel in The Shining.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:45.210
Then it transitions to the Sewers of Derry
with the "The turtle can't help us" graffitied

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.210
on the wall.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:49.960
If you don't know the significance of The
Turtle, an entity in both The Dark Tower and

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.060
IT, I suggest that you check out my last IT
video right here.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:57.560
Then we're invited to the prom scene from
Carrie, Andy Defresne's prison cell in The

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:03.330
Shawshank Redemption, this is Christine, complete
with CQB 241 license plate, these are the

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:07.900
two main locations from The Stand and it all
leads back to The Dark Tower.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.550
If you want to see a Stephen King cinematic
universe, leave a like on this video.

